# Add a feature with the makers

1. List the makers and their options: `npm run make -- --list` (or
   `node shell.mjs make --list --json`).
2. Preview the plan without writing anything, for example:
   `node shell.mjs make feature bookmarks --entity bookmark --dry-run`
   `node shell.mjs make command open-bookmarks --feature bookmarks --dry-run`
   Review the listed files and the plan hash. Existing files are never overwritten.
3. Apply exactly that plan: re-run the same command with `--yes` instead of
   `--dry-run` (ask the user first if the plan touches files outside
   `src/features/<name>/`, locales or the bootstrap registry).
4. The makers write starter tests to `tests/runtime/generated/`; `npm run check`
   runs them with the product tests. Extend them for the new behaviour (real
   services, exact Markdown/data assertions), then run `npm run check`.
5. Verify the command or view in Obsidian with `npm run -s dev:obsidian -- --json`
   (the new command id appears in `commands`).

Rules: features import only from `src/features/api.ts` and application/domain
contracts; UI uses `services.modals`/`services.notices`; Vue files stay under
`presentation/components`. Guide: `docs/development/BUILD-A-FEATURE.md`.
